(root/'README.md').write_text('''# CORP-05 — Alder Community Credit Union

Independent local static research replica in the company / regional credit-union stratum. Fictional brand, original prose and two original local SVG illustrations. Inspired by BECU; no affiliation.

## Source and approval

Approved source: https://www.becu.org/ . Availability verified 2026-11-12T00:52:00.021127+00:00 through Python urllib GET with redirects plus live search/text extraction. These are availability/text observations, not browser verification. Evidence: `pipelines/codex/research/CORP.md` and `pipelines/codex/research/evidence/CORP-http-2026-11-12.json`. Samhith Varma approved verified Codex sources on 2026-11-12 in `metadata/change-log.md`, “Codex Phase A approval (slots 04–06)”. Earlier provisional language in research notes is historical. Active allocation 01–06; 07–10 deferred.

## Run

Open `index.html` directly in a modern browser. Relative links, inline location data, CSS and JS require no server, build, dependency, account or network. Sign-in displays a notice only. No data is submitted, persisted or collected.

## Complete sitemap and mapping

'''+''.join(f'- `{x["local_file"]}` ← {x["url"]}\n' for x in mapped)+'''- `404.html` — protocol-required local recovery page (source arbitrary missing path returned 404).

## Features and datasets

Eight source-mapped pages plus 404. Shared repeated header/utility/primary navigation, breadcrumbs, community/help/footer bands, banking hub, checking benefits and membership explanation, grouped rate guide, support disclosures, contact-channel guide, fictional directory and about story. Two original SVGs. Three inline fictional locations; ten fictional rate rows across four tables; no customer records. Checking FAQ: four disclosures; support: three; contact: three.

Menu has mobile disclosure and Escape focus return. Native disclosures use browser keyboard behavior. Sign-in opens a modal notice with native modal focus containment, Escape dismissal and opener focus return. Location search matches names, services, hours and neighborhoods, announces counts/empty results, and resets. No sensitive fields. Contact is informational: no inquiry form was observed, so none is added. Membership/account opening, messaging, video banking and appointment booking are explicitly unavailable.

Fictional numeric rate tables are an intentional category-content addition: source hub category links were observed, numerical tables were not. Locator filter behavior is inferred, not claimed as a live-source reproduction. No calculator or unsupported account screens.

## Validation and limits

See `generation-metadata.json` and the run evidence at `pipelines/codex/runs/2026-11-13T15-55-36-598Z-build-CORP-05/`. Shared QC is attempted once; actual outcome is recorded there. Static source checks and actual exported JS filter logic are tested separately. Mock DOM tests, if listed, do not establish browser interaction correctness. No screen-reader, real keyboard/browser, zoom, responsive visual, contrast audit or rendered fidelity verification is claimed. WCAG 2.2 AA is a target, not a conformance claim.
''')
(root/'fidelity-notes.md').write_text('''# CORP-05 fidelity notes

## Replicated information architecture

Home → everyday banking → checking; rates; member support → contact; locations; about. The source’s personal-banking, membership, sign-in, support and locations paths inform repeated navigation. Home follows financial well-being → products → learning → community/help bands. Checking follows benefits → rate context → eligibility/opening explanation → FAQ. Rates groups deposits, mortgages/home equity, vehicles and other personal/business products. Contact groups phone, messaging, video, hours/mailing, security and suggestion/media topics. Locations has directory and planning content. About centers member ownership and impact.

## Approximated

Original serif-led editorial headings, burgundy CTAs, cream/sage content bands and a compact utility header approximate a credit-union marketing hierarchy. Exact rendering, source spacing, imagery, color values, breakpoint and responsive order were unavailable in HTTP research. No pixel fidelity claim. Native details approximate source expanded/disclosure clues; compact mobile disclosure approximates navigation states. Source tab markup was observed but individual tab relationships were not verified; direct local navigation is used instead of inventing audience-tab panels.

## Simulated and inferred

Sign-in opens a notice with no credential fields. Membership/opening is explanatory only. Local directory filtering across three invented branches is an inferred approximation to “find nearby locations”; no source input fields were returned. No live map, route, geolocation or appointments. All contact channels are descriptions, not callable links/submission controls.

## Intentionally added

Ten clearly fictional numeric examples in four rate tables supplement the observed category hub. They are not copied/current rates and are not financial advice. Native dialog notice provides an honest endpoint to the observed sign-in affordance. 404 is the protocol-required recovery page. Research banners and explicit simulation notes prevent confusion.

## Omitted

Real trademarks, copied media/prose, real member data, real credentials, financial transactions, applications, membership eligibility decisions, contact inquiry form (not observed), calculators (not inspected), careers (not mapped), external messaging/video/maps and speculative screens. No unsupported audience/business product screens.

## Unverified

Rendered source layout, interactions, mobile menu, exact tab behavior, location widget, account-opening process, contact submissions, current financial rates and full eligibility geography. Static implementation checks and JS tests cannot substitute for browser/assistive technology review. Detailed test outcomes are retained with the run.
''')
